{"name":"Red Sauce Parlour","hex":"#cc3b22","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"sauce","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A liquid (often thickened) condiment or accompaniment to food.","Tomato sauce (similar to US tomato ketchup), as in:"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add sauce to; to season.","To cause to relish anything, as if with a sauce; to tickle or gratify, as the palate; to please; to stimulate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sauce"},{"term":"parlour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of parlor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parlour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sauce","blocks":[{"text":"In cooking, a sauce is a liquid, cream, or semi-solid food, served on or used in preparing other foods. Most sauces are not normally consumed by themselves; they add flavour, texture, and visual appeal to a dish. Sauce is a French word probably from the post-classical Latin salsa, derived from the classical salsus 'salted'. Possibly the oldest recorded European sauce is garum, the fish sauce used by the Ancient Romans, while doubanjiang, the Chinese soy bean paste, is mentioned in Rites of Zhou 20."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Lunch_sauces.jpg/330px-Lunch_sauces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sauce"},{"title":"Parlour","blocks":[{"text":"A parlour is a reception room or public space. In medieval Christian Europe, the \"outer parlour\" was the room where the monks or nuns conducted business with those outside the monastery and the \"inner parlour\" was used for necessary conversation between resident members. In the English-speaking world of the 18th and 19th century, having a parlour room was evidence of social status."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Ca%27_Rezzonico_-_Il_Parlatorio_delle_monache_di_San_Zaccaria_-_Francesco_Guardi.jpg/330px-Ca%27_Rezzonico_-_Il_Parlatorio_delle_monache_di_San_Zaccaria_-_Francesco_Guardi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parlour"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Whisking_sauce-01.jpg/500px-Whisking_sauce-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Whisking_sauce-01.jpg/500px-Whisking_sauce-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A chef whisking a sauce","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhisking_sauce-01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Kolas%C3%A5s_sjudandes_p%C3%A5_spisen.jpg/500px-Kolas%C3%A5s_sjudandes_p%C3%A5_spisen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Kolas%C3%A5s_sjudandes_p%C3%A5_spisen.jpg/1280px-Kolas%C3%A5s_sjudandes_p%C3%A5_spisen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Kolas%C3%A5s_sjudandes_p%C3%A5_spisen.jpg/500px-Kolas%C3%A5s_sjudandes_p%C3%A5_spisen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Caramel sauce","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKolas%C3%A5s_sjudandes_p%C3%A5_spisen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Flickr_avlxyz_4140435178--Salmon_Benedict_on_potato_cake.jpg/500px-Flickr_avlxyz_4140435178--Salmon_Benedict_on_potato_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Flickr_avlxyz_4140435178--Salmon_Benedict_on_potato_cake.jpg/1280px-Flickr_avlxyz_4140435178--Salmon_Benedict_on_potato_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Flickr_avlxyz_4140435178--Salmon_Benedict_on_potato_cake.jpg/500px-Flickr_avlxyz_4140435178--Salmon_Benedict_on_potato_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hollandaise sauce atop a salmon Eggs Benedict","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlickr_avlxyz_4140435178--Salmon_Benedict_on_potato_cake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Sauce_boat.jpg/500px-Sauce_boat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki